WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:04.320
Generally speaking, if you're watching&nbsp;
something with a teen character,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.320 --> 00:00:08.320
they're likely being played by an&nbsp;
adult actor. There are many reasons&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:08.320 --> 00:00:13.040
for this—but some castings truly push&nbsp;
the boundaries of believability. Here&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:13.040 --> 00:00:16.960
are some of the most notable cases of&nbsp;
grown adults playing high schoolers.

00:00:18.160 --> 00:00:23.440
Beverly Hills 90210's cast was a mixed&nbsp;
bag of teens and adults when the show&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:23.440 --> 00:00:28.080
first premiered in 1990. The characters&nbsp;
were supposed to be sophomores in high&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:28.080 --> 00:00:32.960
school during the first season, so a range&nbsp;
of 15 to 17 would have been realistic.

00:00:32.960 --> 00:00:37.360
But most of the cast members were already&nbsp;
in their upper teens when the show began.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:37.360 --> 00:00:42.480
Tori Spelling was 17 when she started out&nbsp;
as Donna Martin, as was Brian Austin Green,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:42.480 --> 00:00:45.280
who was actually playing a&nbsp;
freshman as David Silver.

00:00:45.280 --> 00:00:50.640
Shannen Doherty and Jason Priestley, who played&nbsp;
fraternal twins, Brenda and Brandon Walsh,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:50.640 --> 00:00:55.760
were 20 and 21 years old—while bad boy&nbsp;
Dylan was played by the late Luke Perry,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:55.760 --> 00:00:58.400
who was a whopping 25 at the time.

00:00:58.400 --> 00:01:04.160
The most shocking casting, however, was that&nbsp;
of Gabrielle Carteris as Andrea Zuckerman.

00:01:04.160 --> 00:01:08.160
The character is supposed to be super&nbsp;
smart and way more mature than her peers:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:08.160 --> 00:01:12.160
Andrea focuses on getting ahead&nbsp;
academically instead of partying.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:12.160 --> 00:01:17.440
But Carteris was 29 years old when she&nbsp;
signed on to play 16-year-old Andrea.

00:01:17.440 --> 00:01:20.400
According to reports, Carteris lied about her age&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:20.400 --> 00:01:24.480
and told the casting director she&nbsp;
was "over 21" when she auditioned.

00:01:24.480 --> 00:01:26.080
But in the show's fifth season,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:26.080 --> 00:01:30.400
Carteris' real-life pregnancy forced&nbsp;
the writers to incorporate the pregnancy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:30.400 --> 00:01:35.120
into Andrea's storyline, which led to the&nbsp;
character's eventual exit from the show.

00:01:36.080 --> 00:01:42.160
When Party of Five premiered in 1994, the main&nbsp;
characters consisted of 24-year-old eldest brother&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:42.160 --> 00:01:48.240
Charlie, played by Matthew Fox, 16-year-old&nbsp;
Bailey, played by Scott Wolf, Julia, 15, played&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:48.240 --> 00:01:54.560
by Neve Campbell, 11-year-old Claudia, played by&nbsp;
actress Lacey Chabert, and baby Owen, age one.

00:01:54.560 --> 00:01:58.160
Chabert was obviously in the&nbsp;
same age range as her character,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:58.160 --> 00:02:03.440
as was baby Owen. But Campbell was 21&nbsp;
when the series began, and Fox was 28.

00:02:03.440 --> 00:02:08.640
Scott Wolf was 26 when he landed the role&nbsp;
of Bailey—a full 10 years older than his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:08.640 --> 00:02:12.880
character. Bailey was a rebellious&nbsp;
teen who took on more responsibility&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:12.880 --> 00:02:16.080
after the Salinger parents&nbsp;
were killed in a car accident.

00:02:16.080 --> 00:02:19.440
Later in the storyline, Wolf's&nbsp;
character deals with alcoholism,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:19.440 --> 00:02:23.840
and pulls away from his family. Bailey's&nbsp;
arc is defined by his relationship with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:23.840 --> 00:02:28.560
his on-again-off-again girlfriend Sarah,&nbsp;
played by Jennifer Love Hewitt. In the end,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:28.560 --> 00:02:32.720
perhaps Wolf's maturity helped him capture&nbsp;
the essence of his Bailey counterpart.

00:02:34.465 --> 00:02:39.520
Dawson's Creek had quite a few teenagers among&nbsp;
its original cast when it first aired in 1998.

00:02:39.520 --> 00:02:42.080
Many of the characters were&nbsp;
high school sophomores. And&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:42.080 --> 00:02:46.480
a majority of those starring roles went&nbsp;
to actors of a pretty close age range.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:46.480 --> 00:02:51.040
Michelle Williams was 17 when she&nbsp;
played the 16-year-old Jen Lindley,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:51.040 --> 00:02:56.240
15-year-old Dawson was played by 20-year-old&nbsp;
James Van Der Beek, and 15-year-old Pacey and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:56.240 --> 00:03:02.320
16-year-old Joey were played by a 19-year-old&nbsp;
Joshua Jackson and 18-year-old Katie Holmes.

00:03:02.320 --> 00:03:07.120
But then the McFee siblings arrived and&nbsp;
threw off Dawson's age-appropriate groove.

00:03:07.120 --> 00:03:15.440
"I've always been this complete klutz. Some&nbsp;
things never change." "No. Everything changes."

00:03:16.320 --> 00:03:19.360
In season two, Jack and&nbsp;
Andie McFee joined the gang&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:19.360 --> 00:03:23.600
and all those teenage hormones were&nbsp;
interrupted by 20-something shenanigans.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:23.600 --> 00:03:28.720
Actor Kerr Smith was 26 when he stepped&nbsp;
onto the set of Dawson's Creek as Jack.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:28.720 --> 00:03:34.480
The record, however, goes to Meredith Monroe, who&nbsp;
was 28 years old when she started playing Andie.

00:03:34.480 --> 00:03:37.200
Both siblings are supposed to be just 16.

00:03:37.920 --> 00:03:40.720
On Fox's musical high school comedy Glee,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:40.720 --> 00:03:44.640
it might as well have been a requirement&nbsp;
to be an adult playing a teenager. Most&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:44.640 --> 00:03:48.320
actors were significantly older than the&nbsp;
teenage characters they were playing:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:48.320 --> 00:03:54.800
Lea Michele was 23 when she took on 15-year-old&nbsp;
Rachel Berry, as were Mercedes actor Amber Riley&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:54.800 --> 00:04:00.800
and Quinn actor Dianna Agron. Heather Morris and&nbsp;
Naya Rivera were both 22 when the show began.

00:04:00.800 --> 00:04:04.800
The only one whose age still ended as&nbsp;
a teen was 19-year-old Chris Colfer,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:04.800 --> 00:04:07.360
whose character Kurt is supposed to be 16.

00:04:07.360 --> 00:04:13.200
But the biggest age gap goes to the late Cory&nbsp;
Monteith, who was 27 years old when he was cast&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:13.200 --> 00:04:18.720
as the 15-year-old Finn Hudson. Sure, Monteith&nbsp;
seemed young, but not as young as an actual&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:18.720 --> 00:04:23.360
15-year-old. With the incredible shooting&nbsp;
and rehearsal demands of a show like Glee,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:23.360 --> 00:04:27.760
it's not surprising the producers went&nbsp;
with actors who were all over 18—so&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:27.760 --> 00:04:31.520
that they didn't have to deal with&nbsp;
any minor-centric acting laws.

00:04:31.520 --> 00:04:35.280
Monteith's age afforded him a&nbsp;
unique wealth of life experience,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:35.280 --> 00:04:39.600
especially when compared to some of his&nbsp;
castmates. Before he broke into Hollywood,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:39.600 --> 00:04:44.320
Monteith had worked as a Walmart greeter,&nbsp;
roofer, cab driver, and school bus driver.

00:04:45.280 --> 00:04:50.560
As is the case with so many shows, all of the&nbsp;
kids on Gilmore Girls were played by adults.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:50.560 --> 00:04:55.360
When the show started out, Rory, played by&nbsp;
Alexis Bledel, and her pals are sophomores&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:55.360 --> 00:04:59.600
in high school. Bledel was 19 while&nbsp;
playing her 16-year-old character,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:59.600 --> 00:05:04.640
by far the show's most reasonable age match.&nbsp;
Her main love interests are 16-year-old Dean,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:04.640 --> 00:05:10.480
played by an 18-year-old Jared Padalecki, and&nbsp;
15-year-old Jess, played by a then 23-year-old&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:10.480 --> 00:05:16.560
Milo Ventimiglia . Rory's 16-year-old nemesis&nbsp;
Paris was played by 23-year-old Liza Weil.

00:05:16.560 --> 00:05:21.120
You might think those 23-year-old actors are&nbsp;
pushing it. But the president of the "too old for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:21.120 --> 00:05:27.120
school" club on Gilmore Girls has to be Rory's&nbsp;
BFF Lane Kim, who was played by Keiko Agena.

00:05:27.120 --> 00:05:29.840
"If you could live in any city in&nbsp;
the world you pick Philadelphia?"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:29.840 --> 00:05:34.560
"M. Night Shyamalan lives there." "Who?"&nbsp;
"The guy who directed The Sixth Sense."

00:05:35.440 --> 00:05:42.240
At the time, Agena was 27. With Lorelai Gilmore&nbsp;
being 32, played by a 33-year-old Lauren Graham,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:42.240 --> 00:05:47.600
the actor playing Lane was closer in age to her&nbsp;
best friend's mom than she was to her best friend.

00:05:47.600 --> 00:05:52.080
We can't say Agena didn't pull it off—her&nbsp;
Lane is full of youthful exuberance.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:52.080 --> 00:05:57.120
But there's something undeniably funny about&nbsp;
Graham and Agena being real-world peers,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:57.120 --> 00:05:59.520
playing a mom and a young girl on TV.

00:06:00.000 --> 00:06:05.920
Buffy the Vampire Slayer began in 1997 with main&nbsp;
characters who are supposed to be sophomores in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:05.920 --> 00:06:11.280
high school. Buffy, played by Sarah Michelle&nbsp;
Gellar, was 19 playing a 16-year-old. Willow,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:11.280 --> 00:06:16.880
her witchy best-friend-forever, is also 16,&nbsp;
and was played by 19-year-old Alyson Hannigan.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:16.880 --> 00:06:22.240
Nicholas Brendon was much older, at 26, than&nbsp;
his sophomore character, Xander. The oldest&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:22.240 --> 00:06:27.760
member of the cast was David Boreanaz, who,&nbsp;
at 35, was playing vampire-with-a-soul Angel,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:27.760 --> 00:06:32.880
who is supposed to be about 20 ... or&nbsp;
like 250, depending on how you look at it.

00:06:32.880 --> 00:06:38.400
But the oldest actor playing an actual teenager&nbsp;
was Charisma Carpenter, who at 27 took on the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:38.400 --> 00:06:43.920
role of Cordelia Chase, yet another sophomore.&nbsp;
When Cordelia leaves the Scooby gang in season&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:43.920 --> 00:06:48.640
three for the cast of Angel, they bumped her up&nbsp;
in age a bit, so that it didn't feel so awkward.

00:06:49.600 --> 00:06:53.840
We'll give you one guess as to how old the&nbsp;
characters in Riverdale are supposed to be.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:53.840 --> 00:06:56.320
If you guessed sophomores in high school, you win!

00:06:56.320 --> 00:07:00.480
The cast of Riverdale features a whole&nbsp;
gang of actors in their early 20s playing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:00.480 --> 00:07:06.240
characters who are supposed to be 15 or 16&nbsp;
years old. The only actual teen is KJ Apa,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:06.240 --> 00:07:12.800
who was 19 when the show started out. The other&nbsp;
actors—Lili Reinhart, Ross Butler, Camila Mendes,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:12.800 --> 00:07:20.240
Ashanti Bromfield, Madelaine Petsch, Cole Sprouse&nbsp;
and Casey Cott—all range in age from 20 to 26.

00:07:20.240 --> 00:07:24.000
But the eldest member of the&nbsp;
Riverdale gang is Ashleigh Murray,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:24.000 --> 00:07:29.120
who was 30 when she started playing teen&nbsp;
rocker Josie, of Josie and the Pussycats.

00:07:29.120 --> 00:07:31.840
"They were from your father's gang weren't they?"

00:07:31.840 --> 00:07:34.240
This means that Murray is old enough to have been&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:34.240 --> 00:07:38.640
the target audience for the 2001&nbsp;
Josie and the Pussycats movie.

00:07:38.640 --> 00:07:40.000
How's that for perspective?

00:07:40.960 --> 00:07:46.320
Zombie apocalypse drama The Walking Dead isn't a&nbsp;
teen show, though a lot of teens count themselves&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:46.320 --> 00:07:51.280
as fans. It's a show full of grown adults&nbsp;
fighting for their lives. Occasionally,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:51.280 --> 00:07:56.080
however, kids and teens become entangled&nbsp;
in the violent, bloody fight for survival.

00:07:56.080 --> 00:08:01.280
One character of note is Carl, lead character&nbsp;
Rick Grimes' son, who grows from being a kid&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:01.280 --> 00:08:05.600
to a teen throughout the series. But aside&nbsp;
from Carl's actor, Chandler Riggs, there&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:05.600 --> 00:08:10.720
aren't many teen actors on the show. Much like&nbsp;
other shows in which adults are cast as teens,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:10.720 --> 00:08:15.280
The Walking Dead probably did so because of&nbsp;
the series' super-demanding shooting schedule.

00:08:15.280 --> 00:08:19.680
The most popular teen on The Walking&nbsp;
Dead has likely been Beth Greene,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:19.680 --> 00:08:24.240
fan-favorite Hershel's youngest daughter.&nbsp;
Beth appears in seasons two through five,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:24.240 --> 00:08:29.280
and is supposed to be about 16 years old.&nbsp;
In reality, Beth was played by Emily Kinney,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:29.280 --> 00:08:33.680
who was 26 years old when she was on&nbsp;
the series. Beth's death is a sad one,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:33.680 --> 00:08:38.400
since the character is so sweet and kind, but&nbsp;
hey—them's the breaks on The Walking Dead.

00:08:39.200 --> 00:08:44.320
Smallville tells the story of Superman's high&nbsp;
school days in the Kansas town he grew up in.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:44.320 --> 00:08:48.080
Though the young Clark is supposed to&nbsp;
be 14 years old when the show begins,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:48.080 --> 00:08:52.240
the lead actor, Tom Welling, was 24&nbsp;
years old at the time. But really,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:52.240 --> 00:08:55.680
does age matter when aliens&nbsp;
and superheroes are at play?

00:08:55.680 --> 00:09:00.640
Superman Returns, starring Brandon&nbsp;
Routh, debuted in 2006—smack&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:00.640 --> 00:09:05.040
in the middle of Smallville's run. Returns&nbsp;
centers around a grown-up Superman,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:05.040 --> 00:09:09.680
well into his cape-wearing years, dealing&nbsp;
with mature issues of romance and his career.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:09.680 --> 00:09:14.720
Yet Routh was three years younger than Welling,&nbsp;
then playing Clark Kent as a high schooler.

00:09:14.720 --> 00:09:19.200
By the time the show wrapped up, Welling&nbsp;
was 34 years old. Throw in a 29-year-old&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:19.200 --> 00:09:24.800
Michael Rosenbaum playing a 21-year-old Lex&nbsp;
Luthor, and you've got one "geriatric" cast.

00:09:25.600 --> 00:09:30.960
Of the four main characters on The O.C., only&nbsp;
one started out the show as an actual teenager.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:30.960 --> 00:09:34.080
Mischa Barton was 17 years&nbsp;
old when the series began,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:34.080 --> 00:09:39.680
only a blip older than her character Marissa, who&nbsp;
is, you guessed it, a sophomore in high school.

00:09:39.680 --> 00:09:42.320
Other leads like Seth and Summer were played by&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:42.320 --> 00:09:46.160
23-year-old Adam Brody and&nbsp;
21-year-old Rachel Bilson.

00:09:46.160 --> 00:09:49.440
The oldest member of The&nbsp;
O.C. cast was Ben MacKenzie,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:49.440 --> 00:09:54.240
who was 24 when he started playing Ryan&nbsp;
Atwood. Bad boy Ryan is supposed to be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:54.240 --> 00:09:59.120
the new guy in town who shows the rich kids&nbsp;
of The O.C. how to misbehave and have a good&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:59.120 --> 00:10:03.840
time. At least MacKenzie's age gave his&nbsp;
bad-boy vibe a little more believability.

00:10:04.560 --> 00:10:09.920
Veronica Mars premiered in 2004 with Kristen&nbsp;
Bell playing high school private detective&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:09.920 --> 00:10:15.360
Veronica. In a major departure from teen-show&nbsp;
tradition, Veronica Mars is actually a junior&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:15.360 --> 00:10:19.440
when the show begins. The second season&nbsp;
follows her senior year, while the third&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:19.440 --> 00:10:24.800
chronicles Veronica's freshman year at the&nbsp;
fabulously named Neptune's Hearst College.

00:10:24.800 --> 00:10:30.960
Bell was already well into her 20s when the show&nbsp;
began. In 2004, she was 24 years old, making her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:30.960 --> 00:10:35.680
about seven years older than the character.&nbsp;
By the time the series wrapped, she was 27.

00:10:36.720 --> 00:10:41.280
"I'm heading out of town and&nbsp;
I'm not sure when I'll be back."

00:10:42.000 --> 00:10:46.880
The Veronica Mars film that debuted in&nbsp;
2014 sees the Neptune High gang attend&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:46.880 --> 00:10:52.240
their 10-year high school reunion, even though&nbsp;
their graduation was in 2006. The fourth season,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:52.240 --> 00:10:58.000
which hit Hulu in 2019, is set in that year,&nbsp;
with Veronica presumably around age 32,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:58.000 --> 00:11:01.120
again played by Bell at the age of 39.

00:11:01.120 --> 00:11:05.680
All things considered, Veronica Mars should&nbsp;
be proud of itself. Few teen shows could have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:05.680 --> 00:11:11.200
handled such a disjointed, decade-spanning&nbsp;
existence with as much smoothness as it did.

00:11:12.160 --> 00:11:18.160
Fonzie isn't a high-schooler on Happy Days, but&nbsp;
he does start out as a teenager. The 1970s series&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:18.160 --> 00:11:24.320
created by the late Garry Marshall is set in the&nbsp;
1950s, starring Ron Howard as Richie Cunningham,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:24.320 --> 00:11:29.280
an average high school kid in the Midwest.&nbsp;
His best friend—and the Cunningham's tenant,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:29.280 --> 00:11:36.480
who lives above the garage—is Arthur Fonzarelli,&nbsp;
AKA Fonzie or The Fonz, played by Henry Winkler.

00:11:36.480 --> 00:11:42.000
Fonzie starts out the show at 19 years old, but&nbsp;
Winkler was already way into his 20s when the show&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:42.000 --> 00:11:46.320
began. At 29, the actor was a full&nbsp;
decade older than his character,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:46.320 --> 00:11:51.440
a high school dropout who is seen as the bad&nbsp;
boy of the very traditional 1950s setting.

00:11:51.440 --> 00:11:56.320
Fonzie proves them all wrong, however, when he&nbsp;
earns his high school diploma via night school,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:56.320 --> 00:12:01.200
eventually becoming a teacher. By the&nbsp;
time Happy Days ended, Winkler was 39!

